th</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Marshall Graves</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In the platypus a meiotic chain of ten sex chromosomes shares genes with the bird Z and mammal X chromosomes</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2004</year><volume>432</volume><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>917</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15502814</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nature03021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cattanach</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Beechey</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Autosomal and X-chromosome imprinting</article-title><source>Dev Suppl</source><year>1990</year><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2090432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular links between X-inactivation and autosomal imprinting: X-inactivation as a driving force for the evolution of imprinting?</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>R242</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12646153</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00162-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sharman</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Late DNA replication in the paternally derived X chromosome of female kangaroos</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1971</year><volume>230</volume><fpage>231</fpage><lpage>232</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4926712</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/230231a0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richardson</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Czuppon</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharman</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inheritance of glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase variation in kangaroos</article-title><source>Nat New Biol</source><year>1971</year><volume>230</volume><fpage>154</fpage><lpage>155</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5279473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takagi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preferential inactivation of the paternally derived X chromosome in the extraembryonic membranes of the mouse</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1975</year><volume>256</volume><fpage>640</fpage><lpage>642</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1152998</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/256640a0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xue</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Tian</surname><given-names>XC</given-names></name><name><surname>Du</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubota</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Taneja</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dinnyes</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Levine</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pereira</surname><given-names>LV</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aberrant patterns of X chromosome inactivation in bovine clones</article-title><source>Nat Genet